{"name":"Roaring Twenties","hex":"#b39c9e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Roaring Twenties","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The 1920s, referring to the rapid economic expansion and modernization of the period."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Roaring_Twenties"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roaring Twenties","blocks":[{"text":"The Roaring Twenties, sometimes stylized as Roaring '20s, refers to the 1920s decade in music and fashion, as it happened in Western society and Western culture. It was a period of economic prosperity with a distinctive cultural edge in the United States and internationally, particularly in major cities such as Berlin, Buenos Aires, Santiago, Chicago, London, Los Angeles, Mexico City, New York City, Paris, and Sydney. In France, the decade was known as the années folles, emphasizing the era's social, artistic and cultural dynamism. Jazz blossomed, the flapper redefined the modern look for British and American women, and Art Deco peaked."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Baker_Charleston.jpg/330px-Baker_Charleston.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roaring_Twenties","wikidata":"Q13468437"},{"title":"Roar","blocks":[{"text":"A roar /rɔːr/ is a type of animal vocalization that is loud, deep and resonating. Many mammals have evolved to produce roars and other roar-like vocals for purposes such as long-distance communication and intimidation. These include various species of big cats, bears, pinnipeds, deer, bovids, elephants, and simians."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Christopher_the_Lion_at_Franklin_Park_Zoo_%28January_Edition%29.webm/330px--Christopher_the_Lion_at_Franklin_Park_Zoo_%28January_Edition%29.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roar","wikidata":"Q3177438"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Youthful_radio_expert.png/500px-Youthful_radio_expert.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Youthful_radio_expert.png/1280px-Youthful_radio_expert.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Youthful_radio_expert.png/500px-Youthful_radio_expert.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Early radio in Chicago, 1922","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYouthful_radio_expert.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Chrysler_Building_at_night.JPG/500px-Chrysler_Building_at_night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Chrysler_Building_at_night.JPG/1280px-Chrysler_Building_at_night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Chrysler_Building_at_night.JPG/500px-Chrysler_Building_at_night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Climax of the new architectural style: the Chrysler Building in New York City was built after the European wave of Art Deco reached the United States.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChrysler_Building_at_night.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Felix-pace.jpg/500px-Felix-pace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Felix-pace.jpg/500px-Felix-pace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Felix the Cat, a popular cartoon character of the decade, exhibits his famous pace.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFelix-pace.jpg"},{"srcset"